    "result_text": "All 254 tests pass and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for `POST /api/owners`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it automatically (`GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it).\n\n3. **New function `rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, computes `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`: LAST3 = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, NNNN = `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` zero-padded to 4 digits, and mutates the entity in place.\n\n4. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `assignCustomerCode` step (under `transaction` governance) between `rejectDuplicate` and `save`, so the count reflects the *current* number of owners (the new one isn't saved yet, giving the \"one more than current count\" semantics).\n\n5. **Schema/data** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four `db/*/schema.sql` files, and appended a `NULL` to the hsqldb (test DB) column-less owner seed inserts to keep column counts aligned.\n\nThe global-sequence behavior matches the test: creating \"smithers\" then \"jones\" yields codes `SMI-000N` and `JON-000(N+1)`, since the second create counts the now-persisted first owner.",
